    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Feedback is instrumental for improving performance. In professional environments, feedback has the potential to drive both organizational and individual development. Yet performance management processes are largely ineffectual. Extensive research demonstrates that individuals on both leadership and employee levels lack confidence in existing feedback processes. Peak is a mobile app for professional teams that seeks to transform the way we give, receive, and perceive feedback at work. Rooted in learning science theory, Peak teaches users to define goals that pave a clear pathway for growth, to self-assess performance and progress, and to construct feedback that is informative and conducive to learning. We integrated learnings from academic and user research to design an experience that is 1) mobile, 2) integrated, 3) collaborative, 4) scaffolded, 5) adaptive, 6) ongoing, and 7) personal. We have tested chunked segments of Peak and propose next steps to continue to increase its potential for impact. Our hope is that in putting Peak in the hands of all members of a team and integrating it into everyday work processes, it will push out an organizational culture of feedback and truly transform feedback at work.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
